+# Decouple ioutil from server/interfaces
+
+Replaced ioutil's only uses of `server/interfaces` with local `Committer` and
+`CommittedWriteCloser` interfaces, and removed `//server/interfaces` from its
+BUILD dependencies. The method sets are identical. `CustomCommitWriteCloser`
+keeps its existing name and method set; no exported function returned
+`interfaces.CommittedWriteCloser`, so no alias or caller changes were needed.
+
+Added a regression test covering structural implementation of the local
+interfaces, forwarding the underlying commit, callback order and byte count,
+underlying commit errors, repeated commit rejection, and close forwarding.
+
+## Dependency measurements
+
+The baseline was measured before editing. Both label counts use:
+
+```sh
+bazel query 'deps(//server/util/ioutil)' | wc -l
+```
+
+| Measurement | Before | After |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| Total dependency labels (including sources and implicit dependencies) | 4,576 | 1,630 |
+| First-party dependency labels (`//`) | 289 | 37 |
+| External dependency labels (`@`) | 4,287 | 1,593 |
+| First-party rules, including implicit analyzer rules | 187 | 32 |
+| First-party rules excluding 29 unchanged analyzer/config rules | 158 | 3 |
+| ioutil.go lines (`wc -l`) | 446 | 457 |
+| BUILD lines (`wc -l`) | 27 | 26 |
+| ioutil_test.go lines (`wc -l`) | 275 | 333 |
+
+Query outputs were captured in `/tmp/ioutil-{before,after}-deps.txt` and counted
+with `wc -l`; prefix counts come from the same captured outputs. Rule counts
+were obtained with `kind(".* rule", ...)`: baseline first-party labels were
+saved before editing and classified afterward; the after query was
+`kind(".* rule", deps(//server/util/ioutil)) intersect //...`.
+The unchanged implicit rules are `//:nogo_config`, `//:vet`, `//:vet_actual`,
+and the 26 `//rules/go/analyzer` rules. Thus the survey's 158 → 3 estimate is
+confirmed when those implicit rules are excluded. The remaining three rules
+are ioutil, bytebufferpool, and status.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `gofmt` and `git diff --check`: passed.
+- `bazel query 'rdeps(//..., //server/util/ioutil, 1)'`: failed (exit 7) while
+  fetching the unrelated `+dockerfile_image+default_execution_image`
+  repository. Its `/bin/docker build --no-cache` command timed out. A redundant
+  queued retry was interrupted after this failure was established.
+- Fallback: `bazel query 'attr("deps", "//server/util/ioutil(:ioutil)?", //...)'`
+  succeeded and found 31 direct dependents. This matches all 31 references
+  found by `rg -n 'server/util/ioutil' --glob BUILD`; all are deps entries.
+  Targets are saved in `/tmp/ioutil-direct-rdeps.txt`, with ioutil itself added
+  to `/tmp/ioutil-build-targets.txt`.
+- An initial build invocation supplied both a positional target and
+  `--target_pattern_file`; Bazel rejected it (exit 2). Corrected below.
+- `bazel test --jobs=2 //server/util/ioutil:ioutil_test`: passed (exit 0),
+  including required nogo validation; 1 test target passed, 3,566 actions,
+  1,774.653 seconds.
+- `bazel build --jobs=2 --target_pattern_file=/tmp/ioutil-build-targets.txt`:
+  passed (exit 0): 32 targets, including all 31 direct dependents and their
+  test binaries, plus required nogo validation. 4,012 executed actions,
+  3,316.168 seconds; dependent tests were built without running them.
+
+Long commands run under `nohup`, with logs in `/tmp/ioutil-build-direct.log`
+and `/tmp/ioutil-build-retry.log`.
+
+## Scope and dependency ownership
+
+Only `server/util/ioutil/` and this required report changed. No callers,
+shared dependency files, lockfiles, external modules, or interfaces definitions
+were edited. No external module becomes unused: removing this edge leaves
+interfaces and its entire dependency closure reachable elsewhere.
+Evidence: `rg -l '"//server/interfaces"' --glob BUILD server enterprise | wc -l`
+returns 198 remaining BUILD files with direct users. No dependency cleanup is
+needed for the separate serialized PR.
+
+The unrelated Docker repository failure was not fixed, and dependent tests
+are built but not run; the changed package's tests are run.
+
+To preserve disk space during local compilation, removed approximately 2.06 GiB of old
+large downloaded archives from Bazel's content-addressable archive cache.
+Extracted repositories and build outputs were retained.
